Following this election, Labour lost its Majority Control of the Council, being left with only 17 seats, instead of 18 or more needed for full control, leaving the council in No Overall Control; after Labour HELD one seat, Conservatives RE-GAIN one seat, an Independant WINS one seat and Reform GAINS the remaining eight seats. 

Changes 2024–2026:
*November 2024: Edward Blake (Labour) dies – by-election held February 2025<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jacobs |first1=Bill |title=Sadness after Labour councillor dies after just six months in job |url=https://www.lancashiretelegraph.co.uk/news/24720795.baxenden-labour-councillor-passes-away-six-months-job/ |access-date=31 December 2025 |work=Lancashire Telegraph |date=13 November 2024}}</ref>
*February 2025: David Heap (Conservative) gains by-election from Labour<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Baxenden Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/3439/#2025-02-06 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=31 December 2025}}</ref>
*June 2025: Joyce Plummer (Independent) joins Conservatives<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jacobs |first1=Bill |title=Former Labour finance boss joins council Tory group |url=http://lancashiretelegraph.co.uk/news/25220868.hyndburn-councils-former-finance-boss-joins-tories/ |access-date=31 December 2025 |work=Lancashire Telegraph |date=9 June 2025}}</ref>
*February 2026: Marlene Haworth (Conservative) dies<ref>{{Cite web |last=Jacobs |first=Bill |date=2026-02-05 |title=Tributes paid after death of former Hyndburn Council leader and mayor |url=https://www.lancs.live/news/lancashire-news/tributes-paid-after-death-former-33371818 |access-date=2026-02-05 |website=Lancs Live |language=en}}</ref>
*March 2026: Josh Allen (Conservative) resigns the from the Conservative party.
*April 2026: Andrew Clegg (Labour) defects to the Green Party.

